Modifications for ai-dev-env (Apache License 2.0, §4(b)):

  - File renamed to page_browser.py; installed command name changed to page-browser.
  - CDP endpoint is configurable via BROWSER_CDP_HOST / BROWSER_CDP_PORT instead of
    being hard-coded to 127.0.0.1 with a display-derived port.
  - The WebSocket debugger URL is rewritten to the configured endpoint so the helper
    can be used through the CDP host-rewriting gate.
  - Injected page world name and internal globals renamed
    (rakazo-page-browser -> ai-dev-page-browser, __rakazoPageBrowser -> __aiDevPageBrowser).
  - Default home path changed from /home/rakazo to /home/dev.
  - Uploads are restricted to shared workspace/downloads roots and mapped from
    the dev container's canonical paths to the browser container's mount paths.
  - WebSocket handshake deadlines are configurable for bounded browser shutdown;
    failed handshakes retain the socket reference so callers can close it.
